description:
1. Deeply understand the regional user group profile, clarify the positioning of the product's target audience and the pain points of core users, and in combination with the technological trends of the EMS industry, support the discovery of new opportunities and the development of differentiated software solutions.
2. Continuously monitor regional policies and industry regulations, identify new opportunities arising from policy changes; clarify compliance requirements such as product safety regulations and market access, and assist in promoting compliant sales of products in target markets.
3. Continuously track regional industry trends and competing product dynamics, analyze the advantages and disadvantages of solutions from the perspective of the combination of EMS technology implementation and software solutions, refine differentiated selling points for the marketing end, and provide competitive dimension inputs for PDT product development.
4. Through channels such as distributors, customer interviews, user research, VOC data analysis, regional sales, and customer service, collect and analyze regional product and technology requirements, and drive requirement assessment, implementation, and closed-loop acceptance.

1. Bachelor's degree or above, with majors in computer science, software engineering, electronic engineering, automation, or other related fields preferred;
2. Over 6 years of work experience in software products, with a background in the energy industry's EMS preferred;
3. Fluent in English listening, speaking, reading, and writing, able to independently communicate with overseas clients and conduct requirement interviews as a working language;
4. Possess strong user insight and data analysis capabilities, and be familiar with the entire process of software products from requirements research to implementation;
5. Good XFN communication and coordination skills, as well as project promotion capabilities;
6. Be able to accept overseas business trips (e.g., accumulating more than 3 months per year), adapt to cross-time zone and cross-cultural work environments, with preference given to those with overseas work or study experience.

(1) Identify new business opportunities for EcoFlow product as well as implementing business development initiatives to expand sales channels. Analyzing industrial development, identifying prospects, and evaluating competitors's position in the industry and draw sales strategies for EcoFlow;
(2) Build long term partnership with new solar sales channels in the EU market and focusing on Integrated Commercial and Industrial Energy Storage products;
(3) Maintain strong relationship with the major European solar/ renewable energy distributors;
(4) Responsible for DE region offline sales events, attending exhibitions, and conducting business forums;
(5) Plan and deliver sales and marketing activities to capture business opportunities;
(6) Develop and implement sales strategies to increase EcoFlow market share and complete the sales target.

(1) Min 5+ years relevant experience in sales and business development, preferably in the new energy (solar/battery), power equipment tools, and focusing on Integrated Commercial and Industrial Energy Storage products;
(2) Previous track record and strong network with key solar distributors are desired;
(3) Bachelor or Master’s degree specialized in marketing is preferred;
(4) Self-driven, strong Leadership skills, pragmatic, excellent and open communicator, problem solver;
(5) Positive attitude, solution oriented approach, high cultural sensitivity and able to think in other people’s shoes;
(6) Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English (C1 and above), additional European language fluency will be a plus.

