- Identify new business opportunities for sales of products and implement business development initiatives to expand sales channel, by analyzing industrial development, identifying prospects, and evaluating their positioning in the industry to define sales strategies for EcoFlow.
- Responsible to organize and conduct offline sales events , attending exhibitions, business forum, events at our customers' brick-and-mortar in the states
- Build and maintain solid and long-lasting client relationships including maintaining existing sales channels and developing new sales channels in local markets;
- Plan and deliver sales and marketing activities in order to capture business opportunities;
- Develop and implement strategies to increase the scale of EcoFlow's market sshare and complete the sales target;
Proactively follow up with clients to get feedback to educate the internal team on sales strategy.

- Bachelor's Degree holder or above with 5 years' or above relevant experience in sales and business development, new energy(solar/battery/wind), power equipment tools, RV field experience a plus;
- Proven experience in dealing with customers in retail sales,distribution channels preferred;
- Self-motivated, team player with excellent communication, interpersonal and presentation skills;
- Business travel is required

- Secure new renewable installers, build strong relationships, motivating their sales teams and driving engagement;
- Organize and execute local installer training and promotional events to enhance brand loyalty and willingness to cooperate;
- Expand the installer network within the electrical distribution channel, actively engaging and activating new electricians and installers;
- Conduct in-person follow-up visits to potential installers previously contacted by telesales, helping to drive cooperation;
- Communicate company sales strategies, provide product support and on-site guidance to facilitate sales conversion;
- Spend at least 3–4 days per week on field visits, and report customer feedback and progress to management in a timely manner.

- Strong customer service mindset and excellent communication and coordination skills;
- Minimum 3 year of experience in channel sales or field visits; background in renewable energy or electrical industry preferred
- Able to travel frequently with strong time management skills;
- Proactive, goal-oriented, and highly driven in sales execution;
- Fluent in both English and German;
- Possess a valid driver's license and confident driving ability.

